// wholesale pack tools -- what an agent may do with an application.
//
// ONE TOOL, AND IT IS A READ. An agent may ask what state an application is
// in; it may not decide one. Approving somebody's trade account is a
// Client principal's act with a named decider on the row, and a tool that
// let an agent do it would put "the assistant approved it" into a log that
// is supposed to say who did.

@handler(type="function", name="wholesaleApplicationState")
@executionTime("fast")
@description("The derived state of one wholesale application, folded from its append-only decision log, and what is legal next.")
tool wholesaleState {
  applicationId  string!  @description("The application to fold.")
}
